        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Basement mold is a moisture problem that happens to show up as mold. Find where the water comes from with the foil test, fix condensation with a dehumidifier and seepage from the outside in, and the cleanup becomes a one-time job: scrub the hard surfaces with detergent, throw out the porous ones, dry everything inside 48 hours, and HEPA-vacuum what is left.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Stay inside the EPA's roughly 10-square-foot limit for doing it yourself, skip the bleach-and-paint shortcut, and hold the basement under 50 percent humidity from then on. An air purifier is a sensible addition once the source is handled, but the dehumidifier and the gutters are what keep the mold from coming back.
          </p>
